// A workspace, deliberately, and not a `replace` directive in go.mod.
//
// The README's first install instruction is `go install <module>@latest`, and
// `go help install` says the named module's go.mod "must not contain directives
// (replace and exclude) that would cause it to be interpreted differently than
// if it were the main module". A replace line would break that command for
// everyone.
//
// A workspace redirects the build for anyone working inside this repository,
// while the published go.mod keeps requiring upstream bubbletea. That is
// honest: the copy under third_party is upstream v2.0.8 plus two additive
// js-only files, so a native build is identical either way. Only the
// WebAssembly build needs the copy.
//
// See third_party/bubbletea/PATCHES.md.

go 1.26.5

use (
	.
	./third_party/bubbletea
)
